---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site, emailLink } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the Alphpaca website handles visitor information, contact drafts, and external services."
>
  <section class="container page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy / A clear explanation</span>
    <h1>
      Your visit.
      <br />
      <span class="gold-text">Your information.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-description">
      This website is designed to keep data collection to a minimum. Here’s how
      it works.
    </p>
  </section>
  <article class="container legal-content">
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The Alphpaca website serves static pages. We do not add advertising
      trackers, analytics scripts, cookies, or browser storage. Fonts and brand
      assets are served with the site rather than loaded from third-party font
      services.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is prepared for hosting on GitHub Pages. The hosting provider may
      process technical request information, such as IP addresses, to serve and
      secure the website. See{' '}
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        GitHub’s privacy statement
      </a>{' '}
      for its practices.
    </p>
    <h2>Contacting us</h2>
    <p>
      The contact form only prepares a draft in your email application. It does
      not submit your message to a website server or save it in browser storage.
      You decide whether to send it.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive the information you include and your email
      address. We use that correspondence to respond to your request and discuss
      the work or product you contacted us about. Please avoid sending sensitive
      information in an initial inquiry.
    </p>
    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      External websites and your email provider have their own privacy
      practices. Following an external link or sending an email is subject to
      those providers’ policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about information you have shared with Alphpaca, contact{' '}
      <a href={emailLink('Privacy question')}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
